# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command setreg
usage 1   setreg <reg> <value>          write one of the main CPU's registers
usage 2   setreg <cpu> <reg> <value>    same, on another processor - `cpus` lists them

case writable and read-only registers
target fake
covers 1-2
$ setreg
out 40
Usage: setreg [<cpu>] <register> <value>
status 0
action none
$ setreg A
out 40
Usage: setreg [<cpu>] <register> <value>
status 0
action none
$ setreg A 34
out 24
cpu A = 0x34 (was 0x12).
status 0
action none
$ regs cpu
out 109
the main processor registers:
  PC        = 0x8003
  A         = 0x34
  X         = 0x0340
  P         = 0x34
status 0
action none
$ setreg a 1FF
out 45
A is 8-bit, so 0x1FF does not fit (max 0xFF).
status 1
action none
$ setreg X FFFF
out 28
cpu X = 0xFFFF (was 0x0340).
status 0
action none
$ setreg X 10000
out 50
X is 16-bit, so 0x10000 does not fit (max 0xFFFF).
status 1
action none
$ setreg PC 8000
out 35
cpu's PC is read-only on this core.
status 1
action none
$ setreg Q 1
out 54
cpu has no register named 'Q'. Available: PC, A, X, P.
status 1
action none
$ setreg A zz
out 20
'zz' is not a value.
status 1
action none
$ setreg cpu A 7
out 24
cpu A = 0x07 (was 0x34).
status 0
action none
$ setreg gsu R15 1
out 75
gsu reports its registers but this core cannot write them - see `man cpus`.
status 1
action none
$ setreg gsu
out 40
Usage: setreg [<cpu>] <register> <value>
status 0
action none
$ setreg cop R15 1
out 21
'R15' is not a value.
status 1
action none
$ setreg nope A 1
out 57
cpu has no register named 'nope'. Available: PC, A, X, P.
status 1
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1
$ setreg A 1
out 64
GOLDEN publishes no debug CPUs, so it has no writable registers.
status 1
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ setreg A 1
out 58
No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

case on venusrt
target venusrt
covers 1
$ regs cpu
out 215
CPU registers:
  A         = 0x0001
  X         = 0x0000
  Y         = 0x0000
  S         = 0x01F3
  D         = 0x0000
  PB        = 0x00
  PC        = 0xED30
  DB        = 0x00
  P         = 0x34
  E         = 0x1
status 0
action none
$ setreg NOPE 0
out 77
cpu has no register named 'NOPE'. Available: A, X, Y, S, D, PB, PC, DB, P, E.
status 1
action none
end

